ll satisfy its condition.","oracle_id":"0fd114c4-092b-4e28-b0dc-ef529f3bc73e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you've announced that you're casting a spell, players can't take any actions until you've finished doing so. Notably, opponents can't try to remove your commander to change how many modes you may choose.","oracle_id":"0fd114c4-092b-4e28-b0dc-ef529f3bc73e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you've chosen both modes for the spell, it doesn't matter whether you continue to control a commander. This is true even if you somehow no longer control a commander as you finish casting the spell.","oracle_id":"0fd114c4-092b-4e28-b0dc-ef529f3bc73e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The commander you control doesn't have to be your commander.","oracle_id":"0fd114c4-092b-4e28-b0dc-ef529f3bc73e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"There's no extra bonus if you control more than one commander.","oracle_id":"0fd114c4-092b-4e28-b0dc-ef529f3bc73e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Use the number of cards in the target opponent's hand as Jeska's Will resolves to determine how much {R} to add.","oracle_id":"0fd114c4-092b-4e28-b0dc-ef529f3bc73e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You pay all costs and follow all timing rules for cards played with the permission from the last mode of Jeska's Will. For example, if one of the exiled cards is a land card, you may play it only during your main phase while the stack is empty and only if you have an available land play remaining.","oracle_id":"0fd114c4-092b-4e28-b0dc-ef529f3bc73e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A card with Phyrexian mana symbols in its mana cost is each color that appears in that mana cost, regardless of how that cost may have been paid.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Act of Aggression can target any creature an opponent controls, even one that's untapped.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As you cast a spell or activate an activated ability with one or more Phyrexian mana symbols in its cost, you choose how to pay for each Phyrexian mana symbol at the same time you would choose modes or choose a value for X.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you're at 1 life or less, you can't pay 2 life.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Phyrexian mana is not a new color. Players can't produce Phyrexian mana.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To calculate the mana value of a card with Phyrexian mana symbols in its cost, count each Phyrexian mana symbol as 1.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
